# Director agreement — Prime progress and escalation
Date: 2026-10-29. Source: Director/Prime discussion; direct quotes below.

Director:
"So I have noticed about 80% of the time, we can just push it forward."
"So When it's like just running pack passes, I don't need to know that something broke, builder proposes fix, you think build the plan hand it back and in the next couple of passes it completes. I think I should get a longer report when a page's work finishes."
"Yes, I think this is good, a short update should always be included. So I can read for 30 seconds to a minute. Think to myself "yup no issues here" just give the next prompt to you. So that should be the bottom floor or detail."
"Then anything that requires my judgement or starts conflicting with our design or forking. That is a hard stop until you get my input on it."
"When we are in dev mode where we are solving by pushing info back and forth creating that feedback loop to sync understanding. That is a different kind too."
Director approved the integration proposal, then: "That looks good to me. Pack it up."
"No one is working right now. So pick the models you want to work on this I think grok-2 is free at the moment. Then we can process the returns of grok-1 and claude next."

Prime interpretation approved in that exchange: continue/director-input/develop/
complete are proposed typed review outcomes, not new commands or address axes.
Intelligence judges alignment; compute validates records and enforces declared
holds within supported callers. The 80% observation is not a quota. Routine updates
provide visibility without transferring Prime review responsibility to Director.
Hard stop affects dependent work; independent authorized work can continue.
This records intent; it does not approve arbitrary code or seat changed law.
